Discover the world and creatures of Fangtopia, and learn how to craft your own quirky kingdom.
Spooky cute puzzler Fangtopia launches on PS5 October 26
It&#8217;s nearly time to rise from the crypt and build your kingdom! Our upcoming cozy puzzle game Fangtopia has been lurking in the shadows and is ready to creepy-crawl onto PlayStation 5 on October 26 &#8211; just in time for Halloween!
Fangtopia is a world filled with merry monsters and goofy ghouls, crafted by your own hands. You&#8217;ll put it together piece by piece, placing tiles onto a hex grid that surrounds a creepy castle of your choice. There are no time limits, so you can carefully consider each placement and enjoy forming the world at your own pace. However, there is a tile limit, and you&#8217;ll need to deploy every trick (and treat) in your rotten repertoire if you want to top the leaderboards and perfect your devious domain.&nbsp;
As you place tiles, mysterious portals will appear in the oceans around you. Opening these portals will summon a coterie of creatures that bring even more character to your world – once you&#8217;ve found room for them. Meet grotty gremlins, wily werewolves, bawling banshees and many more. Each has a natural habitat, and when you find them a home, they&#8217;ll reward you by gifting bonus tiles to expand your world. Why not try interacting with them after they&#8217;ve been placed? Perhaps a spooky surprise awaits&#8230;&nbsp;
There are multiple ways to play based on what you enjoy the most. The titular Fangtopia mode includes all of the above and is perfect for a quick session. If you&#8217;re itching for more, Ghoulish mode is for you &#8211; it adds a new tile type in the form of rivers, lets you swap which tile you want to place, and introduces and introduces bigger tile groups that have to be placed together. Your stack is also larger in Ghoulish mode, making for longer, trickier sessions. More modes may emerge from the shadows in future&#8230; keep your eyes peeled for more info in the future.
We&#8217;re so excited to share Fangtopia with all of you. It&#8217;s come a long way from the bones of an idea into a fully formed creation, and we think it&#8217;s going to be the perfect game to cosy up with during the spooky season and beyond. Whether you&#8217;re lounging on your sofa and playing on the big screen on PlayStation 5 or hiding under your blankets in bed with your PlayStation Portal, we hope it&#8217;ll give you a care-free, scare-free time. Draw the curtains, turn off the lights, and lock up your werewolves – we&#8217;ll see you on October 26.
